To download a YouTube video using Rust, you will need to use the `youtube-dl` crate. Here is an example of how to use it to download a video from a URL:
```
use std::fs;

use youtube_dl::Youtubedl;

fn main() {
    let ydl = Youtubedl::new();

    let url = "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ";
    let video_path = "video.mp4";

    ydl.download(url, &video_path);

    fs::copy(video_path, ".").unwrap();
}
```
This code creates a new instance of `Youtubedl`, then downloads the specified video by calling the `download` method and passing in the URL and the path where the video should be saved. The `download` method will automatically extract the video and save it in the appropriate format.

You can also specify options for the download, such as the format, resolution, etc. by passing it as a second argument to the `download` method.
```
ydl.download(url, &video_path, "best", Some("720p"));
```
This will download the best available resolution in 720p format.
